smells.EagerTest:
Refactor the eager test into smaller, focused test methods and extract the repeated parsing logic into a private helper:

1. **Extract shared setup** – create a private method, e.g.,
```java
private Document parseDocument(String html, String baseUri) {
    return Jsoup.parse(html, baseUri);
}
```
2. **Create separate test methods** – one for the `<a>` href assertions and another for the `<img>` src assertion, each invoking the helper:
```java
@Test
public void testHandlesAbsOnProtocolessAbsoluteUris_Href() {
    Document doc1 = parseDocument("<a href='//example.net/foo'>One</a>", "http://example.com/");
    Document doc2 = parseDocument("<a href='//example.net/foo'>One</a>", "https://example.com/");
    Element one = doc1.select("a").first();
    Element two = doc2.select("a").first();
    assertEquals("http://example.net/foo", one.absUrl("href"), "Absolute URL for first <a> element should resolve to http://example.net/foo");
    assertEquals("https://example.net/foo", two.absUrl("href"), "Absolute URL for second <a> element should resolve to https://example.net/foo");
}

@Test
public void testHandlesAbsOnProtocolessAbsoluteUris_ImgSrc() {
    Document doc3 = parseDocument("<img src=//www.google.com/images/errors/logo_sm.gif alt=Google>", "https://google.com");
    assertEquals("https://www.google.com/images/errors/logo_sm.gif", doc3.select("img").attr("abs:src"), "Absolute URL for <img> src should resolve to https://www.google.com/images/errors/logo_sm.gif");
}
```
Each test now focuses on a single logical concern, and the common parsing logic is reused, eliminating the Eager Test smell.

